The interactive basemap uses OpenStreetMap Standard tiles:
https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
Map data: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL).
https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
Visible credit is retained on maps, PNGs and PDF map figures. Tiles are loaded
by the browser for the user's current view; its HTTP cache is respected.
No bulk tile download, offline map archive or server tile proxy is provided.
https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/
The service is best-effort, with no availability guarantee. The bundled country
outlines remain usable without remote tiles. No Esri basemap service is used.

The welcome globe is an original canvas rendering of the bundled Natural Earth /
World Atlas country outlines. It uses no Apple imagery or proprietary globe tiles.
The welcome globe colours countries by access route for illustration only.
Explorer separately shows source survey footprints in red (In-App Access),
and country-level external links in yellow (External Access). Point markers are
not used as a substitute for survey boundaries. The footprint snapshot sources,
licences and generalization are documented in sources/DISCOVERY_COVERAGE.md.
Atmospheric glow, ocean highlights, decorative cloud wisps and stars are original
procedural effects. The clouds are illustrative, not meteorological observations.
No studio artwork, film frames or satellite cloud imagery is incorporated.

